WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:05.970
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and Walking Dead
is finally back!

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:09.760
They’ve been posting a lot of clips since
Comic Con but I was still pretty blown away

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:11.110
with how it all went down.

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:15.080
I’m also re-starting my weekly walking dead
giveaway now, it’s just a weekly amazon

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:17.610
card given to a random subscriber in the comments.

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:22.230
All you have to do to enter is be a subscriber
and leave a comment on this video.

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:25.829
Since there’s so much to talk about I’m
doing top 10 WTF moments, then I’ll do my

00:00:25.829 --> 00:00:28.630
review and talk about the rest of the season.

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:30.919
Careful for spoilers from the episode if you
haven’t seen it yet.

00:00:30.919 --> 00:00:33.690
I’ll wait just a sec...okay, here we go.

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:36.600
Number 10 - Terminus Origin Story

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:40.660
This was a flashback to explain how the Terminus
people got to be the way they are.

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:42.059
How they turned into cannibals.

00:00:42.059 --> 00:00:46.519
They cut it up across the episode and Mary
was the one that narrated the action to Carol,

00:00:46.519 --> 00:00:50.699
but basically a group of thugs came in and
just totally tore them up.

00:00:50.699 --> 00:00:54.539
I feel like there will be a lot of debate
about this, but it’s possible that it’s

00:00:54.539 --> 00:00:59.309
an easter egg for Negan and the Savoirs from
the comics.

00:00:59.309 --> 00:01:05.059
Kirkman and Gimple have said multiple times
that they’re not doing that character yet,

00:01:05.059 --> 00:01:09.280
but that doesn’t mean they can’t squeeze
him in the same way they squeezed Morgan in

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:10.370
at the end.

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:14.140
Gimple actually said something funny on Talking
Dead, he said the the people there got so

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:19.640
detached from what they were doing that it
turned into the office on NBC, like a mundane

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:26.340
workplace sitcom.

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:28.640
Number 9 - Welcome to the Kill Floor

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:32.150
I believe that this was Robin Lord Taylor
here, the guy that Rick gave his watch to

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:33.310
in Season 4.

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:34.890
His name was Sam.

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:38.960
Carol found Rick’s watch later, so even
if this was not Sam, he still came through

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:40.610
terminus at some point.

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:45.840
And then passed through their intestinal tracts.

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:49.770
If you’ve never been on the kill floor where
they carve up cows or pigs, they bleed them

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:51.760
out first in trough’s like that.

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:56.030
The terminus people were turning the Survivors
into their cattle.

00:01:56.030 --> 00:02:01.660
And separately from the flashback scene, slugger
here almost gets Glenn with the bat, twice.

00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:05.670
If feel like that’s one too many times to
be a coincidence, so let’s call that another

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:06.670
Negan Easter Egg.

00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:09.619
If you have read the comics, just please use
spoiler tags in the comments.

00:02:09.619 --> 00:02:14.640
Number 8 - Carol and Tyreese Capture a Terminus
Person

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:23.560
They really wanted to differentiate the Terminus
People as a bad group versus the Survivors,

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:29.571
who also kill but are good people and a family.

00:02:29.571 --> 00:02:35.340
Season 5 is all about them becoming family
in a deeper sense.

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:38.670
Abraham, Eugene and Rosita are still kind
of outsiders.

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:42.260
It seems like they don’t trust them enough
to explain Washington DC, but that’s a whole

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:43.610
other storyline.

00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:50.670
I was really proud of Tyreese, we know exactly
how Carol is going to react in any given situation,

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:54.069
Tyreese was the one hopping on one foot trying
not to crush that guy’s skull.

00:02:54.069 --> 00:02:57.330
They didn’t show it, so I keep thinking
in my head that he did the same thing to that

00:02:57.330 --> 00:02:59.550
Terminus guy that The Mountain did to Oberyn
Martell on Game of Thrones.

00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:03.360
I mean, the minute he threatened Baby Judith’s
life, you knew.

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:06.760
There was no way he was going to make it to
the next episode.

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:09.470
Number 7 - Carol Blows up the Gas Tanks

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:11.880
Carol was definitely the MVP of the episode.

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:14.130
And this was the best practical effect in
the episode.

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:15.650
Probably the most expensive too.

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:21.310
I loved that she went straight into rambo
mode too, no hesitation.

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:24.162
The minute she knew something was up she went
into auto search and destroy.

00:03:24.162 --> 00:03:32.750
During the New York Comic Con panel she was
crying a lot, so everyone thought that meant

00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:33.959
she was going to die.

00:03:33.959 --> 00:03:40.459
But I have seen some of the pictures of them
filming future episodes and I can tell you,

00:03:40.459 --> 00:03:42.780
for at least some of the season, she’s fine.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:47.690
I don’t know if she’s actually going to
die later.

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:48.690
It’s still possible.

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:51.060
They not completely done filming all the episodes.

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:52.620
Number 6 - Machine Gun Rick

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:57.410
From the minute he stabbed those two guards
it was just a marathon of gore till he got

00:03:57.410 --> 00:03:58.530
his hands on the Machine Gun.

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:02.569
And even after they escaped, he wanted to
go back and stomp out the rest.

00:04:02.569 --> 00:04:05.630
I wonder how much longer he would have argued
with them if Carol hadn’t of walked up.

00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:10.070
I don’t think he’s crazy this season,
he’ll still listen to reason.

00:04:10.070 --> 00:04:17.000
But I think a lot of his sanity depends on
Carl and Judith.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:20.410
Did anyone else think about Season 3 when
Rick started clearing the Prison out.

00:04:20.410 --> 00:04:24.039
It was like video game levels of violence
and he had unlimited ammo.

00:04:24.039 --> 00:04:31.539
That was the same episode that they hacked
Herschel’s leg off.

00:04:31.539 --> 00:04:33.699
Number 5 - Eugene and The Cure

00:04:33.699 --> 00:04:37.960
I laughed so hard when Sasha questioned Eugene
and gibberish just started pouring out of

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:38.960
his mouth.

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:43.599
He’s one of those guys that thinks if he
talks fast enough and confuses people they’ll

00:04:43.599 --> 00:04:46.370
forget whatever is going on.

00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:47.599
And it worked.

00:04:47.599 --> 00:04:51.699
Eventually I do think that will be over, they’ll
have to figure out his secret.

00:04:51.699 --> 00:04:54.499
If you’ve read the comics, just please use
spoiler tags when talking about The Cure.

00:04:54.499 --> 00:04:55.499
And when talking about Abraham and Rick.

00:04:55.499 --> 00:04:56.499
Their little trio are still outsiders within
the larger group of Survivors.

00:04:56.499 --> 00:05:01.699
Sasha seems like she’s going to be the one
pushing them for answers.

00:05:01.699 --> 00:05:03.020
Number 4 - Mary vs Carol

00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:06.550
Battle Royal, this was the explainer for those
flashback scenes.

00:05:06.550 --> 00:05:10.849
Scott Gimple said that they wanted to tell
the story of how Terminus became the place

00:05:10.849 --> 00:05:11.849
we’re seeing right now.

00:05:11.849 --> 00:05:12.849
They weren’t always cannibals.

00:05:12.849 --> 00:05:15.629
But they just got pushed too far and snapped.

00:05:15.629 --> 00:05:17.499
Wicked way for Tasha Yar to go.

00:05:17.499 --> 00:05:19.999
I always love when I see her pop up on big
shows.

00:05:19.999 --> 00:05:23.090
She got killed in an episode of Dexter during
season 1 I think too.

00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:25.460
I think she might have been the first human
person Dexter ever killed.

00:05:25.460 --> 00:05:28.569
Maybe Denise Crosby just likes really dark
stories.

00:05:28.569 --> 00:05:43.249
I was really happy that they expanded her
part, she was barely in the finale last year.

00:05:43.249 --> 00:05:45.309
Number 3 - The reunion

00:05:45.309 --> 00:05:47.009
This was the cry-worthy moment.

00:05:47.009 --> 00:05:51.159
Everyone is reunited.

00:05:51.159 --> 00:05:54.440
Rick seems like he’s going to permanently
attach baby judith to his body.

00:05:54.440 --> 00:05:58.839
They’ve been separated ever since the prison
battle.

00:05:58.839 --> 00:06:04.240
Tyreese and Sasha too.

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:09.729
Did anyone else think that Daryl looked kind
of sad watching them, I feel like he was thinking

00:06:09.729 --> 00:06:10.759
about Meryl.

00:06:10.759 --> 00:06:16.470
Families being reunited, regardless of genetic
code they might share, they’re all a big

00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:17.470
family now.

00:06:17.470 --> 00:06:21.089
With the exception of the Washington DC crew.

00:06:21.089 --> 00:06:24.009
Number 2 - Saviors Easter Egg

00:06:24.009 --> 00:06:26.279
The second flashback gave me stronger Negan
vibes.

00:06:26.279 --> 00:06:30.610
I don’t know if they have any other cameos
with these mystery attackers this year, but

00:06:30.610 --> 00:06:35.370
the slicked back hair, the voice and the leather
jacket just scream Negan to me.

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:38.770
Number 1 - Morgan is Back

00:06:38.770 --> 00:06:54.600
This was the real WTF, I think the scene was
only a few seconds long but it did the trick.

00:06:54.600 --> 00:06:57.300
Robert Kirkman got asked about this a couple
days ago during Comic Con.

00:06:57.300 --> 00:07:01.219
He said Morgan was definitely coming back
on the show, but it depended on the actor’s

00:07:01.219 --> 00:07:02.219
schedule.

00:07:02.219 --> 00:07:05.869
That makes me think that Morgan won’t be
a cast regular or anything, but he will have

00:07:05.869 --> 00:07:06.869
one or two more minor cameos.

00:07:06.869 --> 00:07:08.710
The scene just showed him tracking the survivors,
so he’ll find them eventually.

00:07:08.710 --> 00:07:13.050
Let me know though, what was your favorite
moment and when do you think Morgan will be

00:07:13.050 --> 00:07:14.050
back?

00:07:14.050 --> 00:07:18.809
Just a heads up too, based on the teaser for
the next episode, Seth Gilliam will be introduced.

00:07:18.809 --> 00:07:20.969
He’s playing Father Gabriel from the Comics.

00:07:20.969 --> 00:07:24.779
I already did a video explaining him, so I’ll
add a link in the description if you want

00:07:24.779 --> 00:07:25.779
to learn more.

00:07:25.779 --> 00:07:29.919
Andrew J West, the guy who plays Gareth, was
also promoted to series regular.

00:07:29.919 --> 00:07:32.479
So he’s not dead, he’ll be back.

00:07:32.479 --> 00:07:38.020
Overall I gave the episode a solid A for making
such a roaring return to television.

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:41.849
Walking Dead is the most popular cable show
in the world right now, so it’s almost ridiculous

00:07:41.849 --> 00:07:44.939
to expect it to keep one-upping itself every
week.

00:07:44.939 --> 00:07:51.179
That being said, they usually crank all the
knobs to eleven for premieres and finales.

00:07:51.179 --> 00:07:53.719
And this did not disappoint.

00:07:53.719 --> 00:07:57.879
It answered a ton of questions about the characters
and did a good job of explaining what the

00:07:57.879 --> 00:08:08.309
new dynamics of the group will be this year.

00:08:08.309 --> 00:08:12.949
I would have liked to spend more time in the
Terminus Flashbacks but we might get more

00:08:12.949 --> 00:08:15.340
of those when Gareth shows up again.

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:19.160
All things said, Rick is going to be a lot
more fun this year.

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:24.710
But Carol is my MVP right now.

00:08:24.710 --> 00:08:26.889
Let me know if you agree Carol is the biggest
badass.

00:08:26.889 --> 00:08:32.099
And don’t forget, I’ll be doing a Q&amp;A
for this tomorrow, so leave all your questions.

00:08:32.099 --> 00:08:36.140
I’ll announce the winner of this week’s
giveaway during that.

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:39.169
It’s an amazon giftcard just like last year.

00:08:39.169 --> 00:08:40.169
Super simple.

00:08:40.169 --> 00:08:41.169
Right now click here to get that video.

00:08:41.169 --> 00:08:42.169
I’ll add the annotation as soon as I post
it.

00:08:42.169 --> 00:08:44.009
And click here for my top 5 Rick Grimes moments.

00:08:44.009 --> 00:08:46.690
Thanks for watching, now let’s all high
five and I’ll see you tomorrow!

